Project guidance: read agents/project-rules.md. This legacy file is not a separate rules authority.

Optional Agno reference (not an installed AutoScriptor feature):
- Reuse Agent instances; never construct them inside query loops. Start single-agent; Team provides autonomous specialization, Workflow provides explicit sequential/conditional control.
- Agent uses model/instructions/tools; OpenAIChat and DuckDuckGoTools are examples. print_response(stream=True) streams; asynchronous workflows await agent.arun(query).
- Structured output: Pydantic schema passed as output_schema; validate response.content.
- Knowledge: configure vector database, hybrid search and embeddings; set search_knowledge=True. LanceDb/OpenAIEmbedder are examples.
- History requires persistent db, user_id, add_history_to_context=True and num_history_runs. SQLite is development-only; use PostgresDb in production.
- AgentOS hosts agents behind an app; connection URLs and API keys come from environment, never source. Production disables show_tool_calls/debug_mode and handles run failures explicitly.
- Avoid unnecessary f-strings and emoji in examples.

Current external API reference: https://docs.agno.com . No Agno/OpenAI dependency is implied for the project runtime.
